# DevFlow Workflow

This project uses devflow v3.0 phased workflow. The AI assistant must follow these rules:

## Phase Awareness

1. Read `.devflow/state.json` at the start of every conversation to determine the current phase
2. Respect gate checks — do not skip phases or advance without meeting prerequisites
3. Load memory from `.devflow/memory/` for project context

## Core Commands

- **Status**: Check `.devflow/state.json` for current phase, mode, and progress
- **Phase Advance**: Only advance when gate requirements are met (artifact files exist)
- **Memory**: Store important decisions in `.devflow/memory/DECISIONS.md`
- **Lessons**: Record learnings in `.devflow/memory/LESSONS.md`

## Gate Requirements

Artifacts live under `.devflow/<req-id>/`. Each phase's exit gate requires its artifact:

<!-- devflow:generated:artifacts START -->
| Phase | Artifact (Gate) |
|-------|-----------------|
| Phase 0 | 00-strategy.md (G0) |
| Phase 1 | 01-analysis.md (G1; plus manual gate G2) |
| Phase 1.5 | 01b-context.md (G2.5) |
| Phase 2 | 02-design.md (G3) |
| Phase 2.5 | 02a-variants.md (G3.5) |
| Phase 3 | 03-tasks.md (G4, strict mode only) |
| Phase 4 | 04-wave-logs.md (G5) |
| Phase 5 | 05-test-report.md (G6) |
| Phase 6 | 06-review.md (G7) |
| Phase 7 | 07-canary.md (G7.5) |
| Phase 8 | 08-archive.md (G8) |

Mode trimming: `fast` starts at 04-wave-logs.md; `lean` starts at 02-design.md; no 03-tasks.md unless `strict`.
<!-- devflow:generated:artifacts END -->

## Token Compression

When `.devflow/config.yaml` has `caveman.level` set, apply corresponding compression to memory files:
- `lite`: 500 chars per file
- `ultra`: 200 chars per file
- `extreme`: 100 chars per file

## Runtime Detection

This project is configured for Cursor. The adapter bridge is at `adapters/shared/core-bridge.js`.
